### crypto LONG: yesterday's low 95 <= stop 98, setup decided TODAY after the candle completed
  veto fired: true  |  reason: born-dead LONG: signal-day low 95 <= invalidation 98
  verdict: VETO FIRES on the actual code. Under a correct rule it should NOT fire: the extreme is pre-decision, already observed by the decision factors. This is pre-entry movement (detection delay), not setup invalidation.

### crypto SHORT: yesterday's high 104 >= stop 102, setup decided TODAY after the candle completed
  veto fired: true  |  reason: born-dead SHORT: signal-day high 104 >= invalidation 102
  verdict: VETO FIRES on the actual code. Should NOT: same pre-decision double-count.

### CORRECTED rule: post-decision 09:30Z bar low 97.4 <= final stop 98
  veto fired: true  |  reason: corrected born-dead LONG: post-decision extreme crossed final stop 98
  verdict: VETO FIRES — correctly: this is genuine setup invalidation, movement strictly after the decision crossed the actual published stop.

### CORRECTED rule: yesterday's low 95 excluded (pre-decision); post-decision bars hold
  veto fired: false  |  reason: null
  verdict: VETO DOES NOT FIRE — correctly: the completed signal-day candle (strictly before decisionAt) is excluded from the extreme check.

### equity LONG: signal-day (entry-bar) low 95 <= stop 98, entry = that bar's close
  veto fired: true  |  reason: born-dead LONG: signal-day low 95 <= invalidation 98
  verdict: VETO FIRES on the actual code. Should NOT fire as a stop-out: the crossing is pre-entry (intraday, before the close fill) — and the entry contract explicitly disclaims executability ('paper execution is not claimed'). Genuine check would be post-entry sessions only.

